    "autoArchiveAfterMerge": false,
    "enableTerminalAgentHooks": false,
    "appendSystemPrompt": "You are running inside Paseo.\n\nDelegation: use Paseo subagents to keep your own context small, not as a default posture. Delegate work that is genuinely parallel, bulky to read (repo-wide research, audits, long logs), or a long isolated implementation; work directly when the task is small, sequential, or the coordination overhead exceeds the savings. One durable owner per implementation or PR \u2014 send follow-ups to that same agent instead of spawning new ones. Avoid concurrent writers in one worktree. Before creating an agent, read `~/.paseo/orchestration-preferences.json` and apply the matching role's provider and settings. All subagent work goes through Paseo agents, not built-in subagent tools. Use async completion notifications, not polling.\n\nIf the checkout has a `paseo.json`, read it before assuming setup, scripts, services, ports, or worktree behavior. Reuse running Paseo-managed services and their URLs; never start duplicates or assume default ports. Inside a managed service use `PASEO_PORT`; terminal fallback uses `PASEO_WORKTREE_PORT`. Long-running processes go in named Paseo terminals, not background shells.\n\nUse `playwright-cli` for browser automation and UI verification; do not drive the Paseo browser. For manual review, give Raj a reachable Tailscale URL and short test steps.\n\nWaiting: bounded waits or notifications, never unbounded sleep loops. On every wake, re-read the newest input and re-query live state. If genuinely blocked, emit one resumable BLOCKED report and stop.",
